[{"id":111096,"sender_id":690,"sender_full_name":"varkor","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/571df014f488b95cc25c203097ee9377?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20using.20Unicode.20in.20a.20post/near/111096\">#1</a> I tried posting a message containing the Unicode symbol for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">λ</span></span></span></span> (<a href=\"https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/U+1D706\">https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/U+1D706</a>), and I got an error. I had expected that the nForum supported full Unicode?</p>","timestamp":1694961586,"subject":"Error using Unicode in a post","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":111097,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20using.20Unicode.20in.20a.20post/near/111097\">#2</a> which coding are you trying to use? It works for instance for <code>&amp;#955;</code>, see the <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Sandbox\">Sandbox</a></em>.</p>","timestamp":1694961775,"subject":"Error using Unicode in a post","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":111099,"sender_id":690,"sender_full_name":"varkor","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/571df014f488b95cc25c203097ee9377?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20using.20Unicode.20in.20a.20post/near/111099\">#3</a> I am just using the Unicode symbol directly, rather than encoding it using HTML or anything else.</p>","timestamp":1694961821,"subject":"Error using Unicode in a post","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":111104,"sender_id":147,"sender_full_name":"Dmitri Pavlov","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7c66d1b7cad17c58076e0f3d13220d63?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20using.20Unicode.20in.20a.20post/near/111104\">#4</a> Testing: λ (verbatim Unicode character).</p>\n<p>Seems to work!  What error message did you get?</p>","timestamp":1694965539,"subject":"Error using Unicode in a post","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":111108,"sender_id":690,"sender_full_name":"varkor","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/571df014f488b95cc25c203097ee9377?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/Error.20using.20Unicode.20in.20a.20post/near/111108\">#5</a> Sorry, I found the code for the wrong lambda character. The one I actually tried was <a href=\"https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/U+1D706\">this one</a>, i.e. “Mathematical Italic Small Lamda” [sic].</p>","timestamp":1694973075,"subject":"Error using Unicode in a post","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]